1. LangChain open_deep_research
================================================================================

The multi-agent research graph in `backend/vendor/open_deep_research/` is
derived from:

    https://github.com/langchain-ai/open_deep_research
    Copyright (c) 2025 LangChain, Inc.
    MIT License (full text: backend/vendor/open_deep_research/LICENSE)

Modifications by this project are marked in-source with `PATCH(deep-research)`
comments. They are:

  a) configuration.py -- added `model_base_url` and `tavily_api_key` fields so
     the endpoint and search credential travel in the per-request config.

  b) deep_researcher.py -- added `base_url` to the `configurable_fields` of the
     shared model and to all six per-node model configs. Upstream relied on a
     process-global `os.environ["ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL"]` write, which raced across
     concurrent requests using different providers.

  c) utils.py -- replaced a call to `get_api_key_for_model()` with
     `configurable.user_api_key`. The function's only definition is commented
     out upstream, so the call raised `NameError` whenever a Tavily search
     triggered summarisation.

  d) utils.py -- `get_tavily_api_key()` now prefers the per-request config over
     the ambient environment.

